# Fugue No. 8 in D-sharp minor, BWV 853 (J. S. Bach, WTC I)
#
# Character: grave, vocal and intensely concentrated, three voices in
# 4/4, in the old contrapuntal style. The subject rises a fifth
# (D#, A#), turns on its upper neighbour and walks down and back up in
# eighths. There are almost no free episodes: Bach works the subject
# upright, inverted, in augmentation (twice as slow) and in stretto,
# building step by step to the augmented entries at the end. It needs
# a slow, steady, singing pulse and no hurry anywhere.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 58. 87 bars of 4/4 is 348 quarters. Per-fugue track
# times (MusicBrainz track lists): Angela Hewitt (Hyperion, 1998) 5:36,
# about 62; Glenn Gould 5:14, about 66; Sviatoslav Richter 6:31, about
# 53; Rosalyn Tureck (2002 issue) 7:17, about 48. 58 sits between
# Richter and Hewitt.
#
# Structure. Entries found with a pattern search on the voices of the
# Mutopia score (parsed and checked note for note against the MIDI);
# the plan of sections follows the Earsense commentary on this fugue
# (earsense.org, WTC I No. 8), which lists the sections but gives no
# bar numbers. "x.5" is the middle of the bar.
#   1-19   Exposition, four entries, the bass taking two in a row:
#          alto 1 (D-sharp minor), soprano 3.5 (answer), bass 8,
#          bass 12.25 (answer). Cadence in A-sharp minor, bar 19.
#   19-30  Three stretto pairs in the upper voices only:
#          alto 19.5 / soprano 20; soprano 24 / alto 24.25;
#          soprano 25.5 / alto 27.25 (toward G-sharp and C-sharp minor).
#          Cadence in F-sharp major, bar 30.
#   30-44  Re-exposition with the inversion: soprano 30, alto 36 (after
#          a cadence in G-sharp minor, bar 35), bass 44.5 (after a
#          cadence in D-sharp minor, bar 44).
#   44-51  Inverted entries in stretto pairs: bass 44.5 / soprano 45,
#          alto 47.5 / soprano about 49.75 (this last one is varied and
#          I am not sure of it).
#   52-56  Stretto in all three voices a quarter apart, upright (bass
#          52, alto 52.25, soprano 52.5), then inverted (bass 54, alto
#          54.25, soprano 54.5).
#   57-61  A lone entry in the soprano (57.5, with a shortened first
#          note), echoed in the alto (61.5); half cadence on A-sharp.
#   62-80  Augmentation: the bass (62-65), the alto (67.5-70) and at the
#          climax the soprano (77.5-80) sing the subject at half speed,
#          with the subject at normal speed and in varied rhythm around
#          them. Half cadence on A-sharp before the soprano (76).
#   81-87  Coda: a falling sequence in dotted rhythm in all voices, then
#          the final cadence on a D-sharp major chord (Picardy third).

tempo 58

dyn 1 p            # bars 1-19: the exposition, grave and quiet
dyn 19.5 mp        # bars 19-29: after the A-sharp minor cadence, the
                   # first strettos
dyn 30 p           # bars 30-43: after the F-sharp major cadence the
                   # inversion begins, a new (softer) colour
dyn 44 mp          # bars 44-51: after the D-sharp minor cadence, the
                   # inverted strettos
dyn 52 mf          # bars 52-61: three-voice strettos
ramp 62-77 f       # bars 62-77: the augmentation section builds to the
                   # soprano's augmented entry, the climax
dyn 81 mf          # bars 81-87: the coda, a step down after the climax

                   # bars 1-3: the alto's subject sounds alone, no lead needed
lead 3-5 top       # answer, soprano
lead 8-9 bottom    # subject, bass
lead 12-13 bottom  # answer, bass (second bass entry in a row)
lead 19-20 mid     # stretto pair: alto
lead 20-21 top     # stretto pair: soprano
lead 30-31 top     # inversion, soprano
lead 36-37 mid     # inversion, alto (hidden in the middle)
lead 44-45 bottom  # inversion, bass
lead 62 bottom     # augmentation, bass (in bar 63 the bass rises above
lead 64-65 bottom  # the alto for a beat, so that bar is left out)
lead 67-70 mid     # augmentation, alto
lead 77-80 top     # augmentation, soprano: the climax

broaden 76 0.93    # bar 76: hold back on the A-sharp half cadence before
                   # the soprano's augmentation
rit 2 0.7          # the last two bars into the D-sharp major chord
